WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
The age of AI brings immense

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.375
power – but also immense infrastructure
complexity.

3
00:00:08.083 --> 00:00:12.625
As AI workloads scale, data centers face
an overwhelming challenge:

4
00:00:13.208 --> 00:00:16.208
how do we orchestrate every component
for perfect harmony,

5
00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:19.583
predicting and preventing issues
before they even arise?

6
00:00:20.125 --> 00:00:23.708
At OCP, the Open Systems for AI initiative
and Hardware

7
00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:27.291
Management Project are pioneering
intelligent systems management.

8
00:00:27.291 --> 00:00:30.791
That’s the bridge connecting IT
infrastructure – like compute,

9
00:00:30.791 --> 00:00:34.333
storage, and networking –
with the physical environment,

10
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.625
such as power and cooling.

11
00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:40.166
The OCP Hardware Management
Project works to standardize

12
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:43.250
and enhance data center systems management
through initiatives

13
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.625
like the Hardware Management
Module, Hardware Fault Management,

14
00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:51.541
Scalable Cloud Infrastructure Management,
and the Open Rack Management Controller,

15
00:00:51.875 --> 00:00:56.833
aiming to create interoperable, efficient,
and modular management solutions.

16
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.250
These efforts include developing
specifications for system interfaces,

17
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:05.666
fault management
APIs, and rack manager interoperability

18
00:01:05.666 --> 00:01:09.958
to improve remote monitoring,
high availability, and platform

19
00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:13.375
manageability for large-scale data centers
and AI factories.

20
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:19.416
To handle this complexity, Open Compute
champions open standards like DMTF’s

21
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:22.541
Redfish, using it as an ‘out-of-band’

22
00:01:22.541 --> 00:01:25.541
management interface for OCP platforms.

23
00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:30.666
OCP Community Redfish open-source profiles
define a targeted subset

24
00:01:30.666 --> 00:01:34.916
of Redfish resources and properties
to keep systems manageable and consistent.

25
00:01:35.791 --> 00:01:39.541
These profiles ensure tools
can monitor system health and apply

26
00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:43.041
firmware updates
consistently across any vendor’s platform.

27
00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:47.875
This creates a clear management hierarchy,
scaling from individual nodes

28
00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:50.875
to entire AI clusters spanning
multiple racks.

29
00:01:51.291 --> 00:01:56.791
It enables resilient, efficient operations
across complex, distributed workloads.

30
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.541
Our work continues by addressing key gaps,

31
00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:03.875
including hardware abstraction layers
for multi-vendor support.

32
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.750
We are also pioneering AI-driven
automated management

33
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:11.208
using ‘Digital Twins’
for predictive optimization.

34
00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:14.875
From deployment
to continuous monitoring, OCP’s system

35
00:02:14.875 --> 00:02:19.750
management vision transforms complexity
into unparalleled capability.

36
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:24.541
It’s how we ensure open, scalable, and
efficient AI data centers for the future.